  message: "FIXED and merged, dev 908968add9 (PR on branch jgstern-agent/fix/ci-gate-fail-closed).\n\nBoth halves fixed in .woodpecker/woodpecker.yml's pytest step:\n (1) the diff and its exit status are captured separately, and the skip fires\n     ONLY on a successful diff that genuinely reported no .py files;\n (2) the push-event base is validated with git cat-file -e before use, falling\n     back to HEAD^ only when CI_PREV_COMMIT_SHA does not resolve - scoped\n     deliberately, since always diffing HEAD^ undercounts a multi-commit push.\n\nBEHAVIOURAL EVIDENCE, not a proxy. tests/test_ci_pytest_selection_gate.py\nEXECUTES the shell block extracted from the YAML against stub binaries on a\nreplaced PATH (L49) and asserts on whether pytest was actually invoked - a\nproduction-path test, not a source-text assertion. Three new cases, all\nmutation-tested against the real workflow file:\n  - reinstating the one-line diff  -> test_failed_diff_does_not_skip_the_suite FAILS\n  - reinstating the unvalidated base -> test_push_event_falls_back_when_prev_sha_was_rewritten FAILS\n  - restored                        -> 7 passed\nThe third case (test_push_event_keeps_a_resolvable_prev_sha) exists so the fix\nis not indistinguishable from \"always use HEAD^\".\n\nNOT CLAIMED: I have not observed a post-merge push pipeline exercising the\nfixed path in CI, because the fix landed on the same push it would first apply\nto. The next merge to dev is the natural observation point."  # 68cd
